 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "seg-01",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "Today the team deploys a small change to the real users. Priya and I look for a detail in the JSON. After lunch, I check the CSV again. Before the meeting, I review the test suite one more time. The team talks about the build job at the standup. At the table, Maria says, \"I'd like to return this.\" I think, then answer, \"This item is damaged.\" With the team's help, the problem becomes smaller.",
   "tts": "Today the team deploys a small change to the real users. Priya and I look for a detail in the J son. After lunch, I check the C S V again. Before the meeting, I review the test suite one more time. The team talks about the build job at the standup. At the table, Maria says, \"I'd like to return this.\" I think, then answer, \"This item is damaged.\" With the team's help, the problem becomes smaller.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-01.mp3",
   "zh": "今天团队向真实用户部署一个小改动。Priya 和我在JSON 格式里找一个细节。午饭后，我又检查了一遍逗号分隔值。开会前，我又复习了一遍测试套件。团队在站会上讨论了构建任务。桌边，Maria说：\"我想退掉这个。\"我想了想，回答：\"这个商品损坏了。\"在团队的帮助下，问题变小了。",
   "hard": [
    {
     "w": "JSON",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "JSON 格式，用键和值表达结构化数据的文本格式"
    },
    {
     "w": "CSV",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "逗号分隔值，用行列保存表格数据的文本格式"
    },
    {
     "w": "I'd like to return this.",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "我想退掉这个。"
    },
    {
     "w": "This item is damaged.",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "这个商品损坏了。"
    },
    {
     "w": "test suite",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "测试套件，一组一起运行的测试"
    },
    {
     "w": "build job",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "构建任务，把源代码转换成可运行产物的任务"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "seg-02",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "My order is wrong at the shop, and I ask to change it. Priya starts with \"I received the wrong order.\" and I continue with \"Could I get a refund?\" Before the meeting, I review the log file one more time. I parse data so the team can see the change. When I use the deployment job, I ask Maria for advice. I compare the test failure with my notes. The work is not easy, but I keep going.",
   "tts": "My order is wrong at the shop, and I ask to change it. Priya starts with \"I received the wrong order.\" and I continue with \"Could I get a refund?\" Before the meeting, I review the log file one more time. I parse data so the team can see the change. When I use the deployment job, I ask Maria for advice. I compare the test failure with my notes. The work is not easy, but I keep going.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-02.mp3",
   "zh": "我在商店拿错了订单，我请求更换。Priya先说了\"我收到了错误的订单。\"我接着说：\"我可以退款吗？\"开会前，我又复习了一遍日志文件。我解析数据，好让团队看到变化。使用部署任务时，我向 Maria 请教。我把测试失败和我的笔记做了比较。工作不容易，但我继续前进。",
